.TH TUI_HTML_RENDER 3 2026-11-15 "libtuikit 1.2" "libtuikit Manual"
.SH NAME
tui_html_render \- HTML shown as styled terminal text
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <tuikit/htmlrender.h>
.PP
.BI "int tui_html_render(const char *" html ", int " width ", int " ansi ", tui_buf *" out );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR tui_html_render ()
renders an HTML body (a mail, a fragment) as text, reflowed to
.I width
columns (values under 20 mean 20), appended to
.I out
without a trailing newline.
Nothing runs and nothing is loaded: scripts, styles and images are never
touched.
.PP
Supported: b, strong, i, em, u, s, strike, del, code, tt, kbd (bold, italic,
underline, strike, cyan), a, br, hr, p, h1 to h6 (bold), div and the other
block elements, ul, ol (with
.IR start ),
li (nested), blockquote (lines start with
.BR "> " ),
pre (kept as written, split at the column), table with tr, th and td (cells in
columns; the widest column is shortened with an ellipsis, a header row of th
is ruled), img (its alt text in brackets), the named, decimal and hexadecimal
entities, and the colour of an element:
.B style="color:..."
or
.BR "<font color=...>" ,
as #rgb, #rrggbb, rgb() or a basic name; also font-weight, font-style and
text-decoration.
.PP
A link reads
.RB \(lq "text (url)" \(rq
for an http, https or mailto address that is not the text itself; any other
target (javascript:, data:, cid:, a relative one) is not shown.
script, style, head, title, template, object, embed, iframe, applet, svg, math,
select, textarea and comments are dropped with their content.
Unknown tags are ignored, their text kept.
Broken markup (unclosed or mis-nested tags, stray end tags, unfinished tags and
entities, missing optional end tags of li, td, th, tr and p) renders what can
be rendered.
Control characters, bidi overrides and the byte order mark are dropped or
shown as spaces.
.PP
With
.I ansi
0 the text is plain and readable.
With 1 it carries SGR sequences: bold 1, italic 3, underline 4, strike 9, code
36, colour 38;2;r;g;b; each line resets its own and a style open at a line
break is opened again on the next line.
.SH RETURN VALUE
0, or \-1 with
.B errno
set to
.B ENOMEM
(or
.B EINVAL
for a NULL
.IR out ).
A NULL or empty
.I html
renders nothing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tui_mdview_init (3),
.BR tui_buf_init (3),
.BR libtuikit (7)
